# TLM concise pagination revision — scratch proposal

Status: drafted, not rendered or independently reviewed. No canonical files,
metadata, accepted output, or run state were changed. The actual v1 ACCEPTED
run remains historical evidence. A fresh reviewed version-3 run must own the
research addition, authoring, reviews, generation and publication.

## Proposed result

Target 11–12 readable pages, with 10 as the permissible lower end. Preserve the
current type size and Palladio family; solve layout with the content hierarchy
and balanced paragraphs. Do not manufacture pages through blank space, larger
type, standalone title/contents pages or repeated quotations. The existing
23-page expansive study already meets the 20–50-page band; adding the new shared
chronology near its terminal apparatus should yield roughly 24–25 pages, subject
to actual build. Its three developed interpretations and their own four-sense
distillations remain intact.

The same-family predecessor 56 establishes the page-1 map/four-sense table,
page-2 dossier hierarchy and two substantive thematic pages. It is a structural
reference only. No appointments, interpretations or source claims from that
different Sunday enter this draft. No postconciliar proper has been inspected.

| Physical page | Component / function | Planned extent |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Ten-element map, immediately followed by exactly four overview rows | About 300 words plus compact title; no history/status apparatus |
| 2 | Scriptural Date and Location, seven distinct biblical dossiers in Catholic canonical order | About 400 words plus generated date labels; one page only |
| 3 | Themes and Movement: mercy makes the command walkable; one Lord gives a people its life | About 500 substantive words plus short locators |
| 4 | Themes and Movement: intercession carries the common wound; mysteries strengthen fidelity for glory | About 500 substantive words plus short locators |
| 5–10/11 | Developed interleaved commentary, five cross-proper questions | About 2,500 substantive words, approximately 2,875 including heading/locator tokens |
| 11/12 | Scope, references and truthful new-run metadata | Roughly 575 words before chronology-reference additions |

The four front pages are substantive reading, not a four-page preface to the
old five-page PDF. Commentary has been expanded by explaining the accepted
witnesses' reasoning and the consequences of their differences. The draft
contains about 5,300 text tokens counted by a simple word regex after macro-name
removal; that is a sizing estimate including citations/table syntax, not the
profile's final substantive word count. Expect approximately 4,300–4,600
substantive words overall. Final accurate counting belongs to the new author
stage. The page budget remains a hypothesis until actual settled TeX and every
page are inspected.

## Component changes proposed for the new run

- New `sections/synthesis/00-inventory.tex`, manifest key `concise-inventory`,
  kind `front-matter`, synthesis mode, all ten element keys.
- New `sections/synthesis/01-overview.tex`, key `concise-overview`, kind
  `front-matter`, synthesis mode; precisely Literal/Allegorical/Moral/Anagogical.
- New shared `sections/02-scriptural-date-location.tex`, key
  `concise-chronology`, kind `front-matter`, research and synthesis modes. It is
  page 2 in the concise entrypoint and terminal historical apparatus in the
  expansive entrypoint. Same source component and same generated data in both.
- New `sections/synthesis/20-themes-and-movement.tex`, key `concise-themes`,
  kind `front-matter`, synthesis mode, exactly two full physical pages.
- Replace the concise `sections/synthesis/10-study.tex` body with the developed
  interleaved draft, retaining existing key `integrated`, kind
  `integrated-commentary`, synthesis-only. Five functional units remain
  questions across the proper, not a procession of ten abbreviated entries or
  three isolated essays.
- Update concise entrypoint and local format for the dossier macros and zref;
  append the shared chronology to the expansive entrypoint before scope and
  references. Do not move or truncate the expansive interpretations.
- Add generated `research/chronology.toml` and
  `research/chronology-annotations.tex`; add actual adopted source owners to the
  research seal and update research/source audits, bindings and references as
  required by the new research stage.
- Update the schema-2 manifest with the additive presentation contract, current
  dependencies and source-grounded cross-element relations. Add fresh run
  provenance/metadata only from the actual new packet. The old homily's prose
  may remain if fresh author/reviewer comparison confirms it; its metadata,
  source approval, build and visual acceptance must belong to the new run.

Agreed additive declaration:

```toml
presentation_contract = "interpretive-pagination-v1"

[presentation]
inventory = "concise-inventory"
overview = "concise-overview"
chronology = "concise-chronology"
themes = "concise-themes"
commentary = "integrated"
```

The chronology component's references include
`research/chronology-annotations.tex`, and that component imports its generated
definitions exactly once. Each biblical key uses the unchanged generated
`chronodate` / `chronologyannotation` interface. Draft physical markers match
root's supplied `triptych:concise:<role>:start/end` contract, with four sense
markers and commentary start. They do not themselves prove page positions.

## What the added commentary does

1. **The Lord and the hearer:** compares Chrysostom's account of the lawyer's
   improvement with Augustine's alternative initial motive, then relates both
   to healed knowledge, truth held in common and the giver's allegiance.
2. **Command and remedy:** distinguishes following, preservation and cure in
   the three orations; develops Augustine's continuing illumination and
   Bellarmine's practical love. It keeps help distinct from replacement of the
   hearer's agency.
3. **The received people:** develops literal creation versus spiritual heavens,
   Chrysostom's body across generations versus Thomas's common order, and the
   afflicted member versus Daniel's representative intercession.
4. **Offering and accountability:** compares healed fidelity, a common center
   and fulfilled speech at Communion; preserves common obligations versus
   special vows and public sovereignty versus the inward conquest of pride.
5. **The common end:** retains the three readings' distinct four-sense emphases
   and their convergence in the eternal remedy, without turning anagogy into
   another label for present moral improvement.

Every claim in those expansions is traceable to the accepted expansive
components 20, 30, 40, 50 or 60 and their already checked source loci. These draft
derivations do not inherit a new verdict; the future cold reviewer still checks
the claims and the expanded condensation.

## Chronology and missing evidence

The current leaf carries no biblical chronology record because v1 introduced no
biblical dates. Read-only `proper-chronology record` and `annotations` outputs
are now retained here exactly, without `--write`. They cover the seven biblical
elements. The three composed prayers receive no invented biblical date row.

The page-2 order is Psalms 32, 75, 101, 118, Daniel 9, Matthew 22, Ephesians 4.
Repeated or reordered verses within one proper are consolidated. The Daniel
chant remains a selected/rearranged adaptation; the Gospel's embedded citations
are not promoted to three independently appointed extra readings.

The current default corpus gives:

- Four Psalms: a general composition boundary before about 165 B.C.; no date
  specific to each psalm may be inferred from it. No Davidic regnal date may be
  supplied simply because an adjacent Sunday printed one.
- Daniel: a seventy-year duration under historical setting, separately from a
  composition range. Preserve the relation label and do not turn the duration
  into the date of Daniel's prayer or the chant's composition.
- Matthew: six received composition alternatives, and an explicit unresolved
  narrated-event date. Preserve all generated alternatives and that typed
  absence; no date may be supplied from memory, a neighboring proper or a
  publication-local chronological calculation.
- Ephesians: two received composition answers, with their disputed status.

`chronology-source-ids.json` lists the exact adopted chronology source IDs.
The new research worker must independently inspect the displayed sources and
their loci, bind/depend on their real source owners and the controlling corpus
owners, and add the references to both editions. Broad copying of all chronology
files or global guidance into review dependencies is not a substitute for that
ownership audit.

The existing accepted biblical contexts support the present geography/speaker
draft. They do not yet supply a full modern authorship/first-audience account
for every dossier, or an independently checked Gospel event location beyond
the bounded chapter-22 encounter. The new research stage should inspect the
canonical location context and the already registered chronology witnesses for
traditional attribution, audience and place, reporting responsible uncertainty.
That is additional verification work, not permission to invent absent dates.
No new acquisition is presently shown necessary; any exact evidence gap after
that inspection should be escalated to the source owner before prose claims
are expanded. The missing Gospel event date is concrete and must remain visible
unless the canonical corpus itself gains a separately reviewed answer.

## Front-matter feasibility and release boundary

The ten short rows and four short senses should fit page 1 at the established
table size. Page 2 is the tightest page because Matthew retains six dates: start
with the same-family 56 wide Date column, preserve two-tier dossiers, and trim
redundant prose before altering legible type size. The two thematic halves are
balanced at roughly 500 substantive words each and account for every appointed
element; settling line breaks remains an actual build task. Commentary must
start on physical page 5, with final bibliography/metadata inside the total
10–12-page band.

The scratch scaffold intentionally has no new-run metadata and does not pretend
to be a build-ready accepted owner. No proof PDF was produced under this
scratch-only authorization. On root's release, a fresh author must follow its
exact v3 packet, not copy this plan as a substitute for the packet or its review.
